  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The change from Jersey to Apache CXF introduced a behaviour change, when requesting a resource with the Accept-Header set to an empty string. ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "Jersey converted the empty string Accept-Header to \"Accept: ",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "marks": [
            {
             "type": "strong"
            }
           ],
           "text": "/",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "text": "\" and therefore responded to such a request with the corresponding object representation and a HTTP 200 Ok.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "Apache CXF does not modify the header value and therefor looks for a resource method annotated with @Produces(\"\") which can not be found. Therefore CXF returns a HTTP 404 Not Found in this scenario. ",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      }
     ],
     "type": "bulletList"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "According to the HTTP spec at ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://www.w3.org/Protocols/rfc2616/rfc2616-sec14"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://www.w3.org/Protocols/rfc2616/rfc2616-sec14",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " it seems CXF implements the better behaviour, but it should be noted that it is supposed to return a HTTP 406 Not Acceptable instead of a 404.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1
  },
